# Verible rule settings (`verible-verilog-lint --help_rules` lists them).
# Everything is at the defaults except the one rule below.
#
# parameter-name-style wants UpperCamelCase. Every parameter and localparam
# here is ALL_CAPS_SNAKE (LANES, ACT_W, ADDR_CTRL, S_IDLE, ...), which is
# the usual HDL convention, and renaming them all just to satisfy this rule
# would make the code harder to read, not easier. It came up on the first
# lint run (2026-07-11, Verible v0.0-4080-ga0a8d8eb) and is turned off for
# the whole project.
-parameter-name-style
